{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492887,"name":"","username":"LiuChunYin","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/77aa72/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T13:45:15.764Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustom remote MCP OAuth fails before sign-in with: redirect_uri is not allowed by the account configuration. Existing connector Owner Google Tasks MCP remains needsAuth / authentication_required, tools=0. Endpoint: \u003ca href=\"https://tasks-mcp.cecinyin.com/mcp\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eSign in ・ Cloudflare Access\u003c/a\u003e . The server uses Streamable HTTP protected by Cloudflare Access Managed OAuth. Bot diagnostics do not expose the DCR redirect_uris array.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd the remote MCP through Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRequest OAuth authorization on that existing connector.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRegistration fails with the redirect_uri error before the sign-in card opens.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllowlisting the exact /agents/ and then /bot/ callbacks in Cloudflare did not resolve it. No duplicate connector was added; retries have stopped.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOAuth should open the owner sign-in flow, then load MCP tools. Please inspect the failing DCR request and provide the exact redirect_uris array, or correct unintended callback entries. Please confirm the supported callback list for current Grok Bot remote MCP.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot version: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: macOS (darwin)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloudflare allows the following exact HTTPS callback paths on the www subdomain of Cursor:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/agents/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/bot/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe existing Grok web callback is also allowed. Localhost and 127.0.0.1 callback options are enabled. Both added Cursor callbacks saved successfully. No wildcard or custom scheme was added.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official MCP SDK completed token exchange, tools listing, read-only Google calls, refresh and reconnect. Grok web also completed OAuth and actual read-only tool calls. This does not prove Bot compatibility: Bot has not invoked connection_status or list_tasklists because tools never load.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePossibly related: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/aws-mcp-callback-url-issue/170390\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eAWS MCP callback URL issue\u003c/a\u003e . We have not established that our request has the same root cause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo credentials, authorization codes, full authorization URLs, private task contents or raw logs are included.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:20:05.254Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":91,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":431.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/aws-mcp-callback-url-issue/170390","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"AWS MCP callback URL issue","clicks":0},{"url":"https://tasks-mcp.cecinyin.com/mcp","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Sign in ・ Cloudflare Access","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138161,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/1","reactions":[{"id":"heavy_plus_sign","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":492957,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T14:19:42.186Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and for checking the server ahead of time with the official MCP SDK and Grok web. That really narrows things down.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s the full \u003ccode\u003eredirect_uris\u003c/code\u003e array that gets sent during Dynamic Client Registration (it’s the same for desktop and Cloud Agents):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecursor://anysphere.cursor-mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://www.cursor.com/agents/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/code\u003e (Cloud Agents / web)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttp://localhost:8787/callback\u003c/code\u003e (desktop loopback)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop authorizes via entry 3 (localhost loopback), so your Cloudflare settings for entries 2 and 3 are already correct. The \u003ccode\u003e/bot/\u003c/code\u003e callback you added isn’t related to desktop registrations. It’s harmless, but not needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue is entry 1. Cloudflare Managed OAuth only allows https in “Allowed redirect URIs”, so you can’t allowlist \u003ccode\u003ecursor://\u003c/code\u003e there at all, and Cloudflare rejects the entire registration with \u003ccode\u003eredirect_uri is not allowed by the account configuration\u003c/code\u003e. This isn’t caused by your setup. Your server and config aren’t the problem here. This is an issue on our side that we’re tracking. The goal is for registration to only send https and localhost callbacks. Once that ships, your current Cloudflare configuration should work without any changes. I’ll post an update here when we have one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkaround for now: since it’s your server, you can bypass OAuth using a Cloudflare Access service token. In Zero Trust, create a service token, add a Service Auth policy to the app, and connect MCP using the \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Id\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Secret\u003c/code\u003e headers instead of OAuth (the server needs to accept identity from the Access JWT via the service token). If you try it, let me know whether the tools load.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:19:42.186Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":46.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":492999,"name":"","username":"LiuChunYin","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/77aa72/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T14:49:57.228Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for suggesting Cloudflare Service Tokens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot confirms that \u003ccode\u003eAddMcpServer.headers\u003c/code\u003e supports custom HTTP headers. However, we cannot find a secure way for the owner to enter \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Secret\u003c/code\u003e: the connector UI only offers OAuth authentication and account renaming, and the tool schema exposes no secret/vault reference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow can I securely configure this header without putting the secret into chat or model-visible tool arguments?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs there an owner-only settings page, secure credential form, or supported secret reference? Please provide the exact steps for \u003cstrong\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/strong\u003e, rather than Cursor editor’s \u003ccode\u003emcp.json\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is not supported, is there an update on removing the legacy \u003ccode\u003ecursor://\u003c/code\u003e callback from the Bot’s OAuth registration?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:49:57.228Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":6.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138161,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":494321,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T18:32:46.863Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, you dug in the right direction, and I need to correct my previous recommendation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRight now, there’s no safe way in Grok Bot to set a custom HTTP header like \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Secret\u003c/code\u003e. Connectors in Grok Bot authenticate only via OAuth. Tokens are stored on the connector backend, and the Bot calls tools without receiving them. There are no owner-only settings, no separate secrets form, and no secret reference for arbitrary headers in the Grok Bot UI. \u003ccode\u003eAddMcpServer.headers\u003c/code\u003e does exist at the API level, but there’s currently nowhere to enter a secret there safely, not via chat and not via model-visible tool args.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the service token via headers approach I suggested applies to the \u003ccode\u003emcp.json\u003c/code\u003e editor, but not to the current Grok Bot. Sorry about the confusion, that workaround isn’t available in the Bot yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the practical path for you is to remove the legacy \u003ccode\u003ecursor://\u003c/code\u003e callback from the OAuth registration. This is on our side, and we’re tracking it. The goal is still the same, only https and localhost callbacks should be sent during registration, and then your current Cloudflare setup will work without changes. I can’t share an exact timeline, but I’ll reply in this thread when there’s an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T18:32:46.863Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":16.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":138161,"username":"LiuChunYin","name":"","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/77aa72/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":499446,"name":"Charles Wood","username":"Charles_Wood","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/6a8cbe/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-23T21:50:30.203Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/deanrie\"\u003e@deanrie\u003c/a\u003e  \u003ca href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8252/#section-8.3\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRFC 8252: OAuth 2.0 for Native Apps | RFC Editor\u003c/a\u003e says that sending \u003ccode\u003elocalhost\u003c/code\u003e in the list of redirect URIs is NOT recommended, and that the corresponding loopback IPs (\u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e for IPv4, \u003ccode\u003e[::1]\u003c/code\u003e for IPv6) should be used instead. Any idea if that is going to be part of the upcoming improvements? We’re running into this while trying to implement DCR in our own MCP.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T21:52:39.771Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"Charles Wood","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8252/#section-8.3","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"RFC 8252: OAuth 2.0 for Native Apps | RFC Editor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":62466,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":500880,"name":"Vaughan G Aus","username":"Vaughan-g-aus","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/vaughan-g-aus/{size}/122098_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-25T10:56:06.076Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSame issue with Grok Bot connecting to a Cloudflare Access Managed OAuth MCP server.\u003cbr\u003e\nCloudflare rejects the whole DCR request because redirect_uris includes\u003cbr\u003e\ncursor://anysphere.cursor-mcp/oauth/callback. Cloudflare only allows https\u003cbr\u003e\nURIs plus localhost/127.0.0.1 toggles, and has no option for custom schemes.\u003cbr\u003e\nI have allowlisted \u003ca href=\"https://www.cursor.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://www.cursor.com/\u003c/a\u003e* and enabled localhost; registration\u003cbr\u003e\nstill returns 400 “redirect_uri is not allowed by the account configuration”.\u003cbr\u003e\nCloudflare Access is a common gate for internal MCP servers, so this blocks\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot for any business using Zero Trust. Is there a target version?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T10:56:06.076Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"Vaughan G Aus","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.cursor.com/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139751,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/10","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":500890,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-25T11:33:52.129Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/vaughan-g-aus\"\u003e@Vaughan-g-aus\u003c/a\u003e - yep, this is the exact same issue described above. Cloudflare Access Managed OAuth only accepts https in Allowed redirect URIs, plus the localhost or loopback toggles, and you can’t allowlist \u003ccode\u003ecursor://anysphere.cursor-mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/code\u003e there. Because of that, Cloudflare rejects the whole DCR registration. This is on our side, not your config, and we’re tracking it. The goal is that registration only sends https and localhost callbacks, and then your current Cloudflare setup will work with no changes. I can’t share a target version yet, but I’ll update this thread when there’s news.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/charles_wood\"\u003e@Charles_Wood\u003c/a\u003e - thanks, great callout on RFC 8252 §8.3. I passed it to the team as input for the registration flow work, and we’ll keep it in mind when revisiting what we send in \u003ccode\u003eredirect_uris\u003c/code\u003e. I can’t promise a specific implementation yet, like switching from \u003ccode\u003elocalhost\u003c/code\u003e to \u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003e[::1]\u003c/code\u003e, but the team has it noted. If your own MCP can accept loopback in the IP form, that’s the most compatible option right now.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T11:33:52.129Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_